#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:139
msgid "Trust Network Participant Verifier"
msgstr "Verificador del Participante en la red de confianza"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts.md#L143
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/concepts.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:143
msgid "Trusted Service"
msgstr "Servicio de confianza"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts.md#L97
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/concepts.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:97
msgid ""
"Universal verifier applications that support different credential standards "
"are complicated by wide variability in format of the credential payloads, "
"signatures, key formats, and key distribution methods. Public keys formats "
"include x509 certificates, JSON Web Key Sets (JWKS), and DID documents. "
"Signing key distribution methods include API gateways, hosted by issuer at a"
" pre-defined URL, embedded in certificates, and by block-chain based "
"resolution. Establishing root of trust by trust anchor or distributing trust"
" list has been accomplished by API gateway, hosted URL, private "
"dissemination and other bilateral sharing agreements."
msgstr ""
"Las aplicaciones de verificación universales que admiten distintas normas de"
" credenciales se ven complicadas por la gran variabilidad del formato de las"
" cargas útiles de las credenciales, las firmas, los formatos de claves y los"
" métodos de distribución de claves. Los formatos de claves públicas incluyen"
" certificados x509, conjuntos de claves web JSON (JWKS) y documentos DID. "
"Los métodos de distribución de claves de firma incluyen puertas de enlace "
"API, el alojamiento por el emisor en una URL predefinida, la incorporación "
"en certificados y la resolución basada en cadenas de bloques. El "
"establecimiento de la raíz de confianza mediante un ancla de confianza o la "
"distribución de listas de confianza se ha llevado a cabo mediante puertas de"
" enlace API, URL alojadas, difusión privada y otros acuerdos bilaterales de "
"intercambio."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts.md#L148
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/concepts.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:148
msgid "Verifiable Digital Health Certificate"
msgstr "Certificado digital de salud verificable"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts.md#L149
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/concepts.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:149
msgid ""
"Verifiable Digital Health Certificate: A digital representation of a data "
"set comprising a certificate or document, designed for a set of specific "
"clinical or public health use cases which is defined using open, "
"interoperable digital health standards; that contains within, or is "
"associated to, a digital signature which can be verified by the public key "
"of a public-private encryption key pair, and which is issued by a GDHCN "
"Participant."
msgstr ""
"Certificado digital de salud verificable: Representación digital de un "
"conjunto de datos que comprende un certificado o documento, concebida para "
"un conjunto de casos de uso clínicos o de salud pública específicos, que se "
"define mediante normas de salud digital abiertas e interoperables; que "
"contiene una firma digital, o está asociada a ella, que puede verificarse "
"mediante la clave pública de un par de claves de cifrado pública-privada, y "
"que es expedida por un Participante en la GDHCN."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts.md#L99
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/concepts.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:99
msgid ""
"While some variability is expected in an approach that preserves "
"sovereignty, there are opportunities for alignment in key format and "
"distribution for the sake of fostering interoperability. With that goal, we "
"provide a unifying trust list format to assemble and share public key "
"infrastructure for all credential specifications used by existing trust "
"networks. Importantly, this format does not enforce a particular policy "
"framework for participants of the trust network."
msgstr ""
"Si bien cabe esperar cierta variabilidad en un enfoque que preserva la "
"soberanía, existen oportunidades de armonización en el formato y la "
"distribución de las claves con el fin de fomentar la interoperabilidad. Con "
"ese objetivo, proporcionamos un formato unificado de lista de confianza para"
" reunir y compartir la infraestructura de clave pública de todas las "
"especificaciones de credenciales utilizadas por las redes de confianza "
"existentes. Cabe destacar que este formato no impone un marco de políticas "
"concreto a los participantes en la red de confianza."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L276
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:276
msgid ""
"[1] eHealth Network. Interoperability of health certificates – Trust "
"Framework. Version 1.0. 12 March 2021. Last accessed 27 April 2021. [2] "
"eHealth Network. Technical Specifications for Digital COVID Certificates "
"Volume 1. Version V1.0.5. Last accessed 27 April 2021. [3] ETSI EN 319 "
"102-1: Electronic Signatures and Infrastructures (ESI); Procedures for "
"Creation and Validation of AdES Digital Signatures; Part 1: Creation and "
"Validation. Version 1.1.1. 2016. Last accessed 23 April 2021."
msgstr ""
"[1] eHealth Network. Interoperability of health certificates – Trust "
"Framework. Versión 1.0. 12 de marzo de 2021. Última consulta: 27 de abril de"
" 2021. [2] eHealth Network. Technical Specifications for Digital COVID "
"Certificates Volume 1. Versión V1.0.5. Última consulta: 27 de abril de 2021."
" [3] ETSI EN 319 102-1: Electronic Signatures and Infrastructures (ESI); "
"Procedures for Creation and Validation of AdES Digital Signatures; Part 1: "
"Creation and Validation. Versión 1.1.1. 2016. Última consulta: 23 de abril "
"de 2021."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L145
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:145
msgid ""
"A SCA SHOULD NOT use the Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) for their"
" DSCs, due to privacy concerns. GDHCN Participant Verifiers SHOULD NOT use "
"OCSP for verification of the DSCs and SHOULD use CRLs.  It is RECOMMENDED "
"that the GDHCN Participants' Backend performs necessary validation of DSC "
"certificates downloaded from the Trust Network Gateway and only forward a "
"set of trusted and validated DSC to GDHCN Participant Verifiers. GDHCN "
"Participant Verifiers SHOULD NOT perform any revocation checking on DSC in "
"their verification process. One reason for this is to protect the privacy of"
" the holders of Verifiable Digital Health Certificates by avoiding any "
"chance that the use of any particular DSC can be monitored by its associated"
" OCSP responder."
msgstr ""
"Por motivos de privacidad, una SCA NO DEBERÍA utilizar el protocolo de "
"estado de certificados en línea (OCSP) para sus DSC. Los verificadores de "
"los Participantes en la GDHCN NO DEBERÍAN utilizar el OCSP para la "
"verificación de los DSC y DEBERÍAN utilizar listas de revocación de "
"certificados (CRL).  Se RECOMIENDA que el sistema de back-end del "
"Participante en la GDHCN realice la validación necesaria de los certificados"
" DSC descargados de la puerta de enlace a la red de confianza y que solo "
"transmita a los verificadores de los Participantes en la GDHCN un conjunto "
"de DSC validados y de confianza. Los verificadores de los Participantes en "
"la GDHCN NO DEBERÍAN realizar ninguna comprobación de revocación de los DSC "
"en su proceso de verificación. Uno de los motivos es proteger la privacidad "
"de los titulares de Certificados digitales de salud verificables, evitando "
"cualquier posibilidad de que el uso de un DSC concreto pueda ser objeto de "
"seguimiento por parte del servidor OCSP asociado."

