#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:193
msgid ""
"The following table gives guidance on the TNPSCA certificate template in "
"case that a GDHCN Participant decides to operate its own SCA for the DCC "
"system. Bold entries are required (MUST be included in the certificate), "
"italic entries are recommended (SHOULD be included). For absent fields, no "
"recommendations are defined."
msgstr ""
"En el cuadro siguiente se ofrecen orientaciones sobre la plantilla del "
"certificado TNPSCA en caso de que un Participante en la GDHCN decida "
"gestionar su propia SCA para el sistema DCC. Las entradas en negrita son "
"obligatorias (DEBEN incluirse en el certificado) y las entradas en cursiva "
"son recomendadas (DEBERÍAN incluirse). No se definen recomendaciones para "
"los campos ausentes."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L240
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:240
msgid ""
"The following table provides guidance for the GDHCN Participant Backend TLS "
"client authentication certificate. Bold entries are required (MUST be "
"included in the certificate), italic entries are recommended (SHOULD be "
"included). For absent fields, no recommendations are defined."
msgstr ""
"En el cuadro siguiente se ofrecen orientaciones sobre el certificado de "
"autenticación de cliente TLS del sistema de back-end del Participante en la "
"GDHCN. Las entradas en negrita son obligatorias (DEBEN incluirse en el "
"certificado) y las entradas en cursiva son recomendadas (DEBERÍAN "
"incluirse). No se definen recomendaciones para los campos ausentes."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L232
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:232
msgid ""
"The following table provides guidance for the GDHCN Participant Backend "
"upload certificate. Bold entries are required (MUST be included in the "
"certificate), italic entries are recommended (SHOULD be included). For "
"absent fields, no recommendations are defined."
msgstr ""
"En el cuadro siguiente se ofrecen orientaciones sobre el certificado de "
"carga del sistema de back-end del Participante en la GDHCN. Las entradas en "
"negrita son obligatorias (DEBEN incluirse en el certificado) y las entradas "
"en cursiva son recomendadas (DEBERÍAN incluirse). No se definen "
"recomendaciones para los campos ausentes."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L205
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:205
msgid ""
"The following table provides guidance on the DSC certificate template in "
"accordance to [2, Section 5]. Bold entries are required (MUST be included in"
" the certificate), italic entries are recommended (SHOULD be included). For "
"absent fields, no recommendations are defined."
msgstr ""
"En el cuadro siguiente se ofrecen orientaciones sobre la plantilla del "
"certificado DSC de conformidad con [2, sección 5]. Las entradas en negrita "
"son obligatorias (DEBEN incluirse en el certificado) y las entradas en "
"cursiva son recomendadas (DEBERÍAN incluirse). No se definen recomendaciones"
" para los campos ausentes."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L101
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:101
msgid ""
"The GDHCN Participant MUST provide three digital certificates during the "
"registration and identification process:"
msgstr ""
"El Participante en la GDHCN DEBE proporcionar tres certificados digitales "
"durante el proceso de registro e identificación:"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L156
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:156
msgid ""
"The GDHCN Participants and the GDHCN Secretariat will use non-production "
"environments (development, acceptance, testing, etc.) to test the system "
"before they move to production or when new features are released. It is "
"mandatory that public key certificates and the related key material are not "
"reused between the production and the non-production environments. Hence, "
"GDHCN Participants MUST use different public key certificates and private "
"keys for the production and all the non-production environments. This "
"applies to the TNPTLS, TNPUP certificates of the GDHCN Participants and all "
"DSCs. The TNGTA certificates will be different for  production and non-"
"production environments."
msgstr ""
"Los Participantes en la GDHCN y la Secretaría de la GDHCN utilizarán "
"entornos distintos del de producción (desarrollo, aceptación, pruebas, etc.)"
" para probar el sistema antes de pasar a producción o cuando se publiquen "
"nuevas funcionalidades. Es obligatorio que los certificados de clave pública"
" y el material de claves conexo no se reutilicen entre el entorno de "
"producción y los demás entornos. Por consiguiente, los Participantes en la "
"GDHCN DEBEN utilizar certificados de clave pública y claves privadas "
"diferentes para el entorno de producción y para todos los demás entornos. "
"Ello se aplica a los certificados TNPTLS y TNPUP de los Participantes en la "
"GDHCN y a todos los DSC. Los certificados TNGTA serán diferentes para el "
"entorno de producción y para los demás entornos."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L83
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:83
msgid ""
"The GDHCN Participants MUST provide the upload certificate to the GDHCN "
"Secretariat during the initial registration procedure (see Section "
"\"Registration of GDHCN Participant Backends\" for more details). Every "
"GDHCN Participant is responsible for their jurisdiction's data and it must "
"protect the private key that is used for signing the uploads. Other GDHCN "
"Participants can verify the signed data packages using the upload "
"certificates that are provided by the TNG."
msgstr ""
"Los Participantes en la GDHCN DEBEN proporcionar el certificado de carga a "
"la Secretaría de la GDHCN durante el procedimiento de registro inicial (para"
" más detalles, véase la sección \"Registro de los sistemas de back-end de "
"los Participantes en la GDHCN\"). Cada Participante en la GDHCN es "
"responsable de los datos de su jurisdicción y debe proteger la clave privada"
" que se utiliza para firmar las cargas. Los demás Participantes en la GDHCN "
"pueden verificar los paquetes de datos firmados utilizando los certificados "
"de carga proporcionados por la TNG."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L99
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:99
msgid ""
"The GDHCN Secretariat and the GDHCN Participant MUST exchange information on"
" technical contact persons for the on-boarding process. It is assumed that "
"the technical contact persons are legitimated by their GDHCN Participants "
"and identification/authentication is performed through other channels."
msgstr ""
"La Secretaría de la GDHCN y el Participante en la GDHCN DEBEN intercambiar "
"información sobre las personas de contacto técnico para el proceso de "
"integración. Se presupone que las personas de contacto técnico están "
"legitimadas por sus respectivos Participantes en la GDHCN y que la "
"identificación/autenticación se realiza por otros medios."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L190
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:190
msgid ""
"The GDHCN Secretariat checks these requirements when it verifies the Letter "
"of Application (see the onboarding process, step [22])."
msgstr ""
"La Secretaría de la GDHCN comprueba estos requisitos cuando verifica la "
"Carta de solicitud (véase el proceso de integración, paso [22])."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L81
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:81
msgid ""
"The key pair that is used by the GDHCN Participant's Backend for the digital"
" signature of uploaded data packages in the TNG system is called Trust "
"Network Participant upload signature key pair and the corresponding public "
"key certificate is abbreviated by TNPUP certificate. Each Trust Network "
"Certificate brings its own TNPUP certificate, which can be self-signed, or "
"issued by an existing certificate authority, such as a public certificate "
"authority (i.e. a certificate authority that issues certificate in "
"accordance with the CAB-Forum baseline requirements). The TNPUP certificate "
"shall be different from any other certificates used by the GDHCN Participant"
" (i.e. SCA, TLS client or DSCs)."
msgstr ""
"El par de claves que utiliza el sistema de back-end del Participante en la "
"GDHCN para la firma digital de los paquetes de datos cargados en el sistema "
"de la TNG se denomina par de claves de firma de carga del Participante en la"
" red de confianza, y el certificado de clave pública correspondiente se "
"abrevia como certificado TNPUP. Cada certificado de la red de confianza "
"aporta su propio certificado TNPUP, que puede ser autofirmado o expedido por"
" una autoridad de certificación existente, como una autoridad de "
"certificación pública (es decir, una autoridad de certificación que expide "
"certificados de conformidad con los requisitos de referencia del CA/Browser "
"Forum). El certificado TNPUP deberá ser distinto de cualquier otro "
"certificado utilizado por el Participante en la GDHCN (es decir, SCA, "
"cliente TLS o DSC)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L30
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:30
msgid ""
"The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL "
"NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"NOT RECOMMENDED\", "
"\"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\" in this document are to be interpreted as "
"described in BCP 14 (RFC2119, RFC8174) when, and only when, they appear in "
"all capitals, as shown here."
msgstr ""
"Las palabras clave \"DEBE\", \"NO DEBE\", \"OBLIGATORIO\", \"DEBERÁ\", \"NO "
"DEBERÁ\", \"DEBERÍA\", \"NO DEBERÍA\", \"RECOMENDADO\", \"NO RECOMENDADO\", "
"\"PUEDE\" y \"OPCIONAL\" que figuran en el presente documento se "
"interpretarán tal como se describe en BCP 14 (RFC2119, RFC8174) cuando, y "
"solo cuando, aparezcan en mayúsculas, como se muestra aquí."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L178
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:178
msgid ""
"The recommended elliptic curve for EC-DSA is again NIST-p-256 due to its "
"widespread implementation."
msgstr ""
"La curva elíptica recomendada para EC-DSA es, también en este caso, "
"NIST-p-256, debido a su amplia implementación."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L166
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:166
msgid ""
"The requirements from [2, Section 3.3.2] apply. Hence, it is strongly "
"RECOMMENDED that Document Signers use the Elliptic Curve Digital Signature "
"Algorithm (ECDSA) with NIST-p-256 (as defined in appendix D of FIPS PUB "
"186-4). Other elliptic curves are not supported. Due to the space "
"restrictions of the digital health certificate, GDHCN Participants SHOULD "
"NOT use RSA-PSS, even if it is allowed as a fallback algorithm. In case "
"GDHCN Participants use RSA-PSS, they SHOULD use a modulus size of 2048 or "
"max. 3072 bit. SHA-256 SHALL be used as cryptographic hash function (see "
"ISO/IEC 10118-3:2004)."
msgstr ""
"Se aplican los requisitos de [2, sección 3.3.2]. Por consiguiente, se "
"RECOMIENDA encarecidamente que los firmantes de documentos utilicen el "
"algoritmo de firma digital de curva elíptica (ECDSA) con NIST-p-256 (según "
"lo definido en el apéndice D de FIPS PUB 186-4). No se admiten otras curvas "
"elípticas. Debido a las limitaciones de espacio del certificado digital de "
"salud, los Participantes en la GDHCN NO DEBERÍAN utilizar RSA-PSS, aunque "
"esté permitido como algoritmo alternativo. En caso de que los Participantes "
"en la GDHCN utilicen RSA-PSS, DEBERÍAN utilizar un tamaño de módulo de 2048 "
"bits o, como máximo, de 3072 bits. Se DEBERÁ utilizar SHA-256 como función "
"hash criptográfica (véase ISO/IEC 10118-3:2004)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L88
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:88
msgid ""
"The requirements on the technical TNG architecture can be summarized as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""
"Los requisitos de la arquitectura técnica de la TNG pueden resumirse del "
"siguiente modo:"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L70
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:70
msgid ""
"The SCA is defined as the certificate authority that issues DSCs, hence "
"GDHCN Participants that use a multi-tier CA hierarchy (e.g. Root CA -> SCA "
"-> DSCs) MUST provide the subordinate certificate authority that issues the "
"DSCs.  So in that case - if a GDHCN Participant uses an existing certificate"
" authority - the GDHCN system will ignore anything above the SCA -- and "
"whitelist only the SCA as the trust anchor (even though it is a sub-ordinate"
" CA). This is as the ICAO model [[2]](#ref-ehn-dcc-techspec-vol1-2021) only "
"allows for exactly two levels - a 'root' SCA and a single 'leaf' DSC signed "
"by just that SCA. In case a GDHCN Participant operates its own SCA, the "
"GDHCN Participant is responsible for the secure operation and key management"
" of that CA. It must be noted that the SCA acts as the trust anchor for DSCs"
" and therefore, protecting the private key of the SCA is essential for the "
"integrity of the Trust Network environment."
msgstr ""
"La SCA se define como la autoridad de certificación que expide los DSC; por "
"consiguiente, los Participantes en la GDHCN que utilicen una jerarquía de "
"autoridades de certificación de varios niveles (por ejemplo, CA raíz -> SCA "
"-> DSC) DEBEN proporcionar la autoridad de certificación subordinada que "
"expide los DSC.  Así pues, en ese caso, si un Participante en la GDHCN "
"utiliza una autoridad de certificación existente, el sistema de la GDHCN "
"hará caso omiso de todo lo que se encuentre por encima de la SCA e incluirá "
"en la lista blanca únicamente a la SCA como ancla de confianza (aunque se "
"trate de una autoridad de certificación subordinada). Ello se debe a que el "
"modelo de la ICAO [[2]](#ref-ehn-dcc-techspec-vol1-2021) solo admite "
"exactamente dos niveles: una SCA «raíz» y un único DSC «hoja» firmado "
"exclusivamente por esa SCA. En caso de que un Participante en la GDHCN "
"gestione su propia SCA, dicho Participante en la GDHCN es responsable del "
"funcionamiento seguro y de la gestión de las claves de esa autoridad de "
"certificación. Cabe señalar que la SCA actúa como ancla de confianza para "
"los DSC y que, por consiguiente, la protección de la clave privada de la SCA"
" es esencial para la integridad del entorno de la red de confianza."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L74
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:74
msgid ""
"The SCA SHALL NOT issue certificates that are valid longer than the CA "
"certificate itself (see [2, Section 5])."
msgstr ""
"La SCA NO DEBERÁ expedir certificados cuya validez sea superior a la del "
"propio certificado de la autoridad de certificación (véase [2, sección 5])."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L272
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:272
msgid ""
"The TLS certificate of the TNG will be issued by a publicly trusted "
"certificate authority (included in all major browsers and operating systems,"
" following the CAB Forum baseline requirements)."
msgstr ""
"El certificado TLS de la TNG será expedido por una autoridad de "
"certificación de confianza pública (incluida en todos los principales "
"navegadores y sistemas operativos y que cumpla los requisitos de referencia "
"del CA/Browser Forum)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L91
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:91
msgid ""
"The TNG maintains a trust list of the TNPSCA certificates that is signed "
"with the TNGTA private key."
msgstr ""
"La TNG mantiene una lista de confianza de los certificados TNPSCA firmada "
"con la clave privada TNGTA."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L61
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:61
msgid ""
"The TNG uses a whitelist where the TLS certificates of GDHCN Participant "
"Backends are added after their successful registration. Only GDHCN "
"Participant Backends that authenticate themselves with a private key that "
"corresponds to a certificate from the whitelist can establish a secure "
"connection to the TNG."
msgstr ""
"La TNG utiliza una lista blanca a la que se añaden los certificados TLS de "
"los sistemas de back-end de los Participantes en la GDHCN tras su registro "
"satisfactorio. Solo los sistemas de back-end de los Participantes en la "
"GDHCN que se autentiquen con una clave privada correspondiente a un "
"certificado de la lista blanca pueden establecer una conexión segura con la "
"TNG."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L89
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:89
msgid ""
"The TNG uses mutual TLS authentication to establish an authenticated "
"encrypted connection with the GDHCN Participant Backends. Therefore, the TNG"
" maintains a whitelist of registered TNPTLS client certificates."
msgstr ""
"La TNG utiliza la autenticación TLS mutua para establecer una conexión "
"cifrada y autenticada con los sistemas de back-end de los Participantes en "
"la GDHCN. Para ello, la TNG mantiene una lista blanca de los certificados de"
" cliente TNPTLS registrados."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L56
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:56
msgid ""
"The TNG uses Transport Layer Security (TLS) with mutual authentication to "
"establish an authenticated encrypted channel between the GDHCN Participant's"
" Backend and the Trust Network Gateway environment and utitlize its API. "
"Therefore, the TNG holds a TLS server certificate, abbreviated TNGTLS - and "
"the GDHCN Participant's Backends hold a TLS client certificate – abbreviated"
" TNPTLS. Certificate templates are provided in Section \"Certificate "
"Templates\"."
msgstr ""
"La TNG utiliza el protocolo de seguridad de la capa de transporte (TLS) con "
"autenticación mutua para establecer un canal cifrado y autenticado entre el "
"sistema de back-end del Participante en la GDHCN y el entorno de la puerta "
"de enlace a la red de confianza, y para utilizar su API. Para ello, la TNG "
"dispone de un certificado de servidor TLS, abreviado como TNGTLS, y los "
"sistemas de back-end de los Participantes en la GDHCN disponen de un "
"certificado de cliente TLS, abreviado como TNPTLS. Las plantillas de "
"certificados figuran en la sección \"Plantillas de certificados\"."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L90
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:90
msgid ""
"The TNG uses two digital certificates (TNGTLS and TNGTA) with two distinct "
"key pairs. The private key of the TNGTA key pair is maintained offline (not "
"on the online components of the TNG)."
msgstr ""
"La TNG utiliza dos certificados digitales (TNGTLS y TNGTA) con dos pares de "
"claves distintos. La clave privada del par de claves TNGTA se mantiene fuera"
" de línea (no en los componentes en línea de la TNG)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L85
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:85
msgid ""
"The TNG verifies the authenticity and integrity of the uploaded data with "
"the TNPUP certificate before it is provided to other GDHCN Participants."
msgstr ""
"La TNG verifica, con el certificado TNPUP, la autenticidad y la integridad "
"de los datos cargados antes de ponerlos a disposición de otros Participantes"
" en la GDHCN."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L63
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:63
msgid ""
"The TNG will also use a TLS certificate that allows the GDHCN Participant "
"Backends to verify that they are indeed establishing a connection to the "
"“real” TNG and not some malevolent entity posing as TNG. The TNGTLS "
"certificate will be issued from a publicly trusted CA (included in all major"
" browsers). It is the responsibility of the GDHCN Participants to verify "
"that their connection to the TNG is secure (for example by checking the "
"fingerprint of the TNGTLS certificate of the server connected to against the"
" one provided post registration)."
msgstr ""
"La TNG también utilizará un certificado TLS que permita a los sistemas de "
"back-end de los Participantes en la GDHCN verificar que efectivamente están "
"estableciendo una conexión con la TNG «real» y no con una entidad "
"malintencionada que se haga pasar por la TNG. El certificado TNGTLS será "
"expedido por una autoridad de certificación de confianza pública (incluida "
"en todos los principales navegadores). Corresponde a los Participantes en la"
" GDHCN verificar que su conexión con la TNG es segura (por ejemplo, "
"comprobando que la huella digital del certificado TNGTLS del servidor al que"
" se conectan coincide con la proporcionada tras el registro)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L49
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:49
msgid ""
"The TNG works as a data hub that allows the exchange of signed data packages"
" for GDHCN Participants. In the current phase, the signed data packages "
"contain the DSC that are used by the GDHCN Participants. This allows other "
"GDHCN Participant Backends to fetch them and distribute the information to "
"their validation apps. Even if the DSCs are already signed by the SCA, this "
"approach allows to extend the system later to allow Backends the upload of "
"different, potentially unsigned, content (like validation rules)."
msgstr ""
"La TNG funciona como nodo central de datos que permite el intercambio de "
"paquetes de datos firmados entre los Participantes en la GDHCN. En la fase "
"actual, los paquetes de datos firmados contienen los DSC utilizados por los "
"Participantes en la GDHCN. Ello permite que los sistemas de back-end de "
"otros Participantes en la GDHCN los obtengan y distribuyan la información a "
"sus aplicaciones de validación. Aunque los DSC ya estén firmados por la SCA,"
" este enfoque permite ampliar posteriormente el sistema para que los "
"sistemas de back-end puedan cargar otros contenidos, posiblemente no "
"firmados (como reglas de validación)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L14
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:14
msgid ""
"The trust model of the GDHCN framework is a Public Key Infrastructures "
"(PKI). Each GDHCN Participant maintains one or more Signing Certificate "
"Authority (SCA), certificates of which are relatively long lived. The SCA "
"issues public key certificates for the short lived, Document Signers (i.e. "
"signers for digital health certificates), which are called Document Signer "
"Certificates (DSCs). The SCA acts as a trust anchor such that relying GDHCN "
"Participants can use the SCA certificate to validate the authenticity and "
"integrity of the regularly changing DSC certificates. Once validated, the "
"GDHCN Participant can provide these certificates (or just the public keys "
"contained therein) to their validation applications."
msgstr ""
"El modelo de confianza del marco de la GDHCN es una infraestructura de clave"
" pública (PKI). Cada Participante en la GDHCN mantiene una o varias "
"Autoridades de certificación de firma (SCA), cuyos certificados tienen una "
"vida útil relativamente larga. La SCA expide certificados de clave pública "
"para los firmantes de documentos, de vida útil corta (es decir, los "
"firmantes de certificados digitales de salud), que se denominan certificados"
" de firmante de documentos (DSC). La SCA actúa como ancla de confianza, de "
"modo que los Participantes en la GDHCN que confían en ella pueden utilizar "
"el certificado de la SCA para validar la autenticidad y la integridad de los"
" certificados DSC, que cambian periódicamente. Una vez validados, el "
"Participante en la GDHCN puede proporcionar estos certificados (o únicamente"
" las claves públicas que contienen) a sus aplicaciones de validación."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
