#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/concepts_did_v1.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_did_v1.md:7
msgid ""
"The unified format DID method selected is did:web, a method to retrieve DID "
"Documents via existing web (https) infrastructure​. ​The did:web identifiers"
" have the form ​. Resolution is accomplished by https GET against the URL "
"which is formed from this identifier by​ . For example "
"did:web:example.com:my:path would resolve a DID Document from the URL ​. "
"Additional did methods may be supported in the future."
msgstr ""
"El método DID de formato unificado seleccionado es did:web, un método para "
"obtener documentos DID a través de la infraestructura web (https) "
"existente​. ​Los identificadores did:web tienen la forma ​. La resolución se"
" realiza mediante una solicitud https GET a la URL que se forma a partir de "
"este identificador mediante​ . Por ejemplo, did:web:example.com:my:path "
"resolvería un documento DID a partir de la URL ​. En el futuro podrán "
"admitirse otros métodos DID."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_did_v1.md#L5
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_did_v1.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/concepts_did_v1.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_did_v1.md:5
msgid ""
"The unified format is based on the Decentralized Identifiers (DIDs) v1.0 "
"specification. DIDs are globally unique identifier in the form of URIs. The "
"URI scheme includes a method name which corresponds to a standard method by "
"which a DID Document can be resolved. This DID Document is a structured "
"JSON-LD which captures each existing public key (regardless of X.509 or JWK "
"format used) by the members of a trust network in a common format. It allows"
" additional metadata (such as intended purpose and key identifiers) to be "
"added to existing keys with changing the underlying keys themselves​. It "
"provides means to publish and cryptographically sign a master lists of keys "
"recognized used by a trust network."
msgstr ""
"El formato unificado se basa en la especificación Decentralized Identifiers "
"(DIDs) v1.0. Los DID son identificadores únicos a nivel mundial en forma de "
"URI. El esquema URI incluye un nombre de método que corresponde a un método "
"normalizado mediante el cual puede resolverse un documento DID. Este "
"documento DID es un JSON-LD estructurado que recoge en un formato común cada"
" una de las claves públicas existentes (con independencia de que se utilice "
"el formato X.509 o JWK) de los miembros de una red de confianza. Permite "
"añadir metadatos adicionales (como la finalidad prevista y los "
"identificadores de clave) a las claves existentes sin modificar las propias "
"claves subyacentes​. Ofrece un medio para publicar y firmar "
"criptográficamente listas maestras de las claves reconocidas y utilizadas "
"por una red de confianza."

