#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L41
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:41
msgid ""
"The backbone of this data exchange is the functionality of the current "
"connector library which connects to the gateway and provides for the "
"consumer the most necessary functionalities. This library is enhanced by the"
" functionality to connect multiple gateways instead of one."
msgstr ""
"La base de este intercambio de datos es la funcionalidad de la actual "
"biblioteca de conectores, que se conecta a la puerta de enlace y proporciona"
" al consumidor las funcionalidades más necesarias. Esta biblioteca se amplía"
" con la funcionalidad de conectarse a varias puertas de enlace en lugar de a"
" una sola."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L28
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:28
msgid ""
"The current gateway design is focused on the trust establishment between "
"“National Backends” in terms of a system operated/owned by a national health"
" authority. This can be a script, a fully automated solution or a manual "
"process, which is able to connect the gateway trustfully and able to do "
"uploads and downloads of the content. What other concrete solutions are "
"behind is not in scope of the gateway itself. Within the DDCC scope, the "
"term “National Backend” is worded too sharply, because there can be other "
"parties which can be connected with their publishing system to a gateway in "
"the trust network. Therefore the term “national backend” should be "
"understood within this scope more as “Trusted Party” in terms of an attendee"
" which has received access to a trusted gateway. The trusted gateway or the "
"federator acts then as well as “Trusted Party” to other gateways."
msgstr ""
"El diseño actual de la puerta de enlace se centra en el establecimiento de "
"la confianza entre «sistemas de back-end nacionales», entendidos como "
"sistemas operados por una autoridad sanitaria nacional o de su propiedad. "
"Puede tratarse de un script, de una solución totalmente automatizada o de un"
" proceso manual capaz de conectarse a la puerta de enlace de forma fiable y "
"de cargar y descargar el contenido. Las soluciones concretas que haya detrás"
" quedan fuera del alcance de la propia puerta de enlace. En el ámbito de la "
"DDCC, el término «sistema de back-end nacional» resulta demasiado "
"restrictivo, ya que puede haber otras partes que conecten su sistema de "
"publicación a una puerta de enlace de la red de confianza. Por consiguiente,"
" en este ámbito, el término «sistema de back-end nacional» debería "
"entenderse más bien como «parte de confianza», es decir, un participante que"
" ha obtenido acceso a una puerta de enlace de confianza. A su vez, la puerta"
" de enlace de confianza o el federador actúan también como «parte de "
"confianza» respecto de otras puertas de enlace."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L138
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:138
msgid ""
"The current trust model of the DCC Gateway supports only the connection of "
"multiple backends and the exchange of content between them (see below)."
msgstr ""
"El modelo de confianza actual de la puerta de enlace del DCC solo admite la "
"conexión de varios sistemas de back-end y el intercambio de contenido entre "
"ellos (véase más abajo)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L241
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:241
msgid ""
"The data format of the federated data should always contain a federation "
"wrapper with the information of federationID, Domain and resource type."
msgstr ""
"El formato de los datos federados debería contener siempre un envoltorio de "
"federación con la información de federationID, Domain y tipo de recurso."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L108
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:108
msgid ""
"The DDCC specification provides interoperable standards for exchanging "
"metadata content such as trusted references, trusted certificates and signer"
" certificates with systems via a Trust Network Gateway. This metadata is "
"managed through Trusted Systems which will need a connection/proxying or "
"facade service with the Trust Network Gateway (“TNG Mediator”). This "
"mediator must be onboarded and trusted by the operator of the TNG before "
"upload or download of content is possible. Technically this can be a script,"
" a backend system or an OpenHIM mediator. The main tasks of this kind of "
"software is to establish a mTLS connection with the gateway, sign the "
"uploaded content (e.g. CMS Cryptographic Message Syntax) and upload signed "
"DSCs, revocation entries or releasing business rules. The procedures used in"
" background is out of scope. There may be manual release processes, "
"automatic decisions or other processes, however it is crucial to ensured "
"that the trusted channel and the security of the used certificates for "
"upload/tls connection are not compromised."
msgstr ""
"La especificación DDCC proporciona normas interoperables para intercambiar "
"contenido de metadatos, como referencias de confianza, certificados de "
"confianza y certificados de firmantes, con sistemas a través de una puerta "
"de enlace a la red de confianza. Estos metadatos se gestionan mediante "
"sistemas de confianza que necesitarán un servicio de conexión, de proxy o de"
" fachada con la puerta de enlace a la red de confianza («mediador de la "
"TNG»). Este mediador debe ser integrado y considerado de confianza por el "
"operador de la TNG antes de que sea posible cargar o descargar contenido. "
"Técnicamente, puede tratarse de un script, de un sistema de back-end o de un"
" mediador OpenHIM. Las principales tareas de este tipo de software son "
"establecer una conexión mTLS con la puerta de enlace, firmar el contenido "
"cargado (por ejemplo, mediante la sintaxis de mensajes criptográficos CMS) y"
" cargar DSC firmados, entradas de revocación o publicar reglas de negocio. "
"Los procedimientos utilizados en segundo plano quedan fuera del alcance. "
"Puede haber procesos de publicación manuales, decisiones automáticas u otros"
" procesos; no obstante, es fundamental garantizar que no se vean "
"comprometidos el canal de confianza ni la seguridad de los certificados "
"utilizados para la carga o la conexión TLS."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L309
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:309
msgid ""
"The Entry will be onboarded in the Gateway and signed by the trust anchor."
msgstr ""
"La entrada se integrará en la puerta de enlace y será firmada por el ancla "
"de confianza."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L180
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:180
msgid ""
"The federator is designed as a new sub component which can be hosted as "
"microservice or within the gateway in one deployment. This behavior can be "
"configured during the installation. Overall the federator offers the "
"functionality for automated download of gateway or federation content. The "
"downloaded content is stored in the gateway database to provide the content "
"to the gateways federation endpoints. Trusted parties can download from "
"these endpoints then the federated data."
msgstr ""
"El federador se ha diseñado como un nuevo subcomponente que puede alojarse "
"como microservicio o dentro de la puerta de enlace en un mismo despliegue. "
"Este comportamiento puede configurarse durante la instalación. En general, "
"el federador ofrece la funcionalidad de descarga automatizada del contenido "
"de puertas de enlace o de federaciones. El contenido descargado se almacena "
"en la base de datos de la puerta de enlace para ponerlo a disposición de los"
" puntos de conexión de federación de la puerta de enlace. A continuación, "
"las partes de confianza pueden descargar los datos federados desde estos "
"puntos de conexión."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L67
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:67
msgid ""
"The gateway content can be used to establish trust between attendees which "
"are just loosely coupled, for example Verifier Devices which are known by "
"Trusted Party A, but not directly known by Trusted Party B."
msgstr ""
"El contenido de la puerta de enlace puede utilizarse para establecer la "
"confianza entre participantes que solo están vinculados de forma laxa, por "
"ejemplo, dispositivos de verificación conocidos por la parte de confianza A,"
" pero no conocidos directamente por la parte de confianza B."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L268
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:268
msgid ""
"The routes for POST, PUT and DELETE will be modified by profiles to make "
"them configurable. This allows it to switch off the data upload, which is "
"especially for the primary-secondary/combined sources use case. Within this "
"setup, no TNPUP certificates need to be onboarded."
msgstr ""
"Las rutas POST, PUT y DELETE se modificarán mediante perfiles para que sean "
"configurables. Ello permite desactivar la carga de datos, lo que resulta "
"especialmente útil en los casos de uso primario-secundario y de fuentes "
"combinadas. En esta configuración, no es necesario integrar certificados "
"TNPUP."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L259
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:259
msgid ""
"The signer information endpoints must be configurable by a profile to be "
"switched on and off the routes. This is necessary to maintain backwards "
"compatibility with the EU DCC Gateway. In the DDCC context these routes are "
"deactivated."
msgstr ""
"Los puntos de conexión de información de firmantes deben poder configurarse "
"mediante un perfil para activar y desactivar las rutas. Ello es necesario "
"para mantener la compatibilidad con versiones anteriores de la puerta de "
"enlace del DCC de la UE. En el contexto de la DDCC, estas rutas están "
"desactivadas."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L37
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:37
msgid ""
"The TNG should realize this enhancement of the current implementation of "
"DCCG with the purpose to create a network between multiple gateways for "
"exchanging health record associated public key material, value sets and "
"business rules between different parties (authority, non-authority, "
"commercial). In this architecture a gateway can connect to any other gateway"
" by manually configuring the list of connections and trust relationships. To"
" manage the connections and their download behavior a new component "
"federator is introduced. The federator is a microservice which acts as an "
"automated download client between two gateways and fulfills all "
"responsibilities of trusted data exchange."
msgstr ""
"La TNG debería llevar a cabo esta mejora de la implementación actual de la "
"DCCG con el fin de crear una red entre varias puertas de enlace para "
"intercambiar material de clave pública asociado a registros de salud, "
"conjuntos de valores y reglas de negocio entre distintas partes "
"(autoridades, entidades que no son autoridades, entidades comerciales). En "
"esta arquitectura, una puerta de enlace puede conectarse a cualquier otra "
"puerta de enlace mediante la configuración manual de la lista de conexiones "
"y de relaciones de confianza. Para gestionar las conexiones y su "
"comportamiento de descarga se introduce un nuevo componente, el federador. "
"El federador es un microservicio que actúa como cliente de descarga "
"automatizada entre dos puertas de enlace y cumple todas las "
"responsabilidades del intercambio de datos de confianza."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L149
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:149
msgid ""
"The trust model doesn’t support raw public keys due to security reasons "
"especially in cases where:"
msgstr ""
"El modelo de confianza no admite claves públicas sin procesar por motivos de"
" seguridad, especialmente en los casos en que:"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L125
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:125
msgid ""
"The trust model of the gateway is based on the PKI certificate governance of"
" the DCC Gateway. All security relevant items are uploaded in signed CMS "
"format and secured by different kinds of PKI certificates as defined by the "
"PKI certificate governance. The central items of the trust model are the SCA"
" to protect the Document Signer Certificates and the CMS messages to protect"
" the uploaded content."
msgstr ""
"El modelo de confianza de la puerta de enlace se basa en la gobernanza de "
"certificados de PKI de la puerta de enlace del DCC. Todos los elementos "
"relevantes para la seguridad se cargan en formato CMS firmado y están "
"protegidos por distintos tipos de certificados de PKI, según lo definido en "
"la gobernanza de certificados de PKI. Los elementos centrales del modelo de "
"confianza son la SCA, que protege los certificados de firmantes de "
"documentos, y los mensajes CMS, que protegen el contenido cargado."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L19
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:19
msgid ""
"The Trust Network Gateway (TNG) specifications in this document are designed"
" to support the DDCC specification, which acts as bridging/umbrella "
"specification for various health records like digital COVID certificates "
"(e.g., EU’s DCC, SMART Health Cards, DIVOC, and ICAO). This specification "
"builds on the EU Digital Covid Certificate Gateway by extending it in "
"several important ways:"
msgstr ""
"Las especificaciones de la puerta de enlace a la red de confianza (TNG) que "
"figuran en el presente documento están concebidas para dar soporte a la "
"especificación DDCC, que actúa como especificación de enlace o marco para "
"diversos registros de salud, como los certificados COVID digitales (por "
"ejemplo, el DCC de la UE, SMART Health Cards, DIVOC e ICAO). Esta "
"especificación se basa en la puerta de enlace del certificado COVID digital "
"de la UE y la amplía en varios aspectos importantes:"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L118
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:118
msgid ""
"The Trust Network Gateway consists of the DCC Gateway enhanced by callback "
"mechanisms and additional trust list sources, a new federator component with"
" the download client, a federation API, a proxy for outgoing calls and an "
"interface to the routes of the different services."
msgstr ""
"La puerta de enlace a la red de confianza consta de la puerta de enlace del "
"DCC, mejorada con mecanismos de devolución de llamada y fuentes adicionales "
"de listas de confianza; un nuevo componente federador con el cliente de "
"descarga; una API de federación; un proxy para las llamadas salientes, y una"
" interfaz con las rutas de los distintos servicios."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L77
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:77
msgid ""
"The Trust Network Gateway purpose is to enable the secured and trusted "
"exchange of data within a trust network."
msgstr ""
"La finalidad de la puerta de enlace a la red de confianza es permitir el "
"intercambio seguro y fiable de datos dentro de una red de confianza."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L254
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:254
msgid ""
"The trusted party table (see chapter 4.2.3.1, EU DCC Gateway) is enhanced "
"with a new certificate type “TRUSTANCHOR” in the API call for trust lists "
"these new types appearing. To distinguish between a federator and a normal "
"trusted party, a type (“TP”, “FEDERATOR”,”GATEWAY”)  for the trusted item is"
" introduced. To distinguish between different domains of certificates, the "
"table also gets a new column ''DOMAIN”, which has the default content "
"“DCC''. Other content can be in the moment “ICAO”, “DIVOC” and “SHC”. The "
"domain appears in the trustlist routes."
msgstr ""
"La tabla de partes de confianza (véase el capítulo 4.2.3.1, puerta de enlace"
" del DCC de la UE) se amplía con un nuevo tipo de certificado, "
"«TRUSTANCHOR»; estos nuevos tipos aparecen en la llamada a la API para las "
"listas de confianza. Para distinguir entre un federador y una parte de "
"confianza normal, se introduce un tipo («TP», «FEDERATOR», «GATEWAY») para "
"el elemento de confianza. Para distinguir entre distintos dominios de "
"certificados, la tabla también recibe una nueva columna, ''DOMAIN”, cuyo "
"contenido predeterminado es “DCC''. Por el momento, otros contenidos "
"posibles son «ICAO», «DIVOC» y «SHC». El dominio aparece en las rutas de las"
" listas de confianza."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L278
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:278
msgid ""
"The trusted references are URLs which are uploaded by the Trust Network "
"Participants to propagate their service endpoint about value sets, business "
"rules and other content for interoperability. Within the trusted references "
"are just public GET methods allowed. Authorization must be covered by trust "
"mediators, if necessary."
msgstr ""
"Las referencias de confianza son URL que cargan los Participantes en la red "
"de confianza para dar a conocer sus puntos de conexión de servicio relativos"
" a conjuntos de valores, reglas de negocio y otros contenidos con fines de "
"interoperabilidad. En las referencias de confianza solo se permiten métodos "
"GET públicos. La autorización, de ser necesaria, debe correr a cargo de los "
"mediadores de confianza."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L170
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:170
msgid ""
"The usage of the OID can limit the scope of a Document Signer Certificate "
"during the verification process (if supported by the verifier app). For "
"instance, fraudulent vaccination certificates issued by test centers, will "
"not be valid, as it is signed by an DSC limited to test result certificate "
"issuers."
msgstr ""
"El uso del OID puede limitar el alcance de un certificado de firmante de "
"documentos durante el proceso de verificación (si la aplicación del "
"verificador lo admite). Por ejemplo, los certificados de vacunación "
"fraudulentos expedidos por centros de pruebas no serán válidos, ya que "
"estarán firmados por un DSC limitado a los emisores de certificados de "
"resultados de pruebas."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L271
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:271
msgid ""
"The ValueSet and Business Rules endpoints must be configurable by "
"configuration of profiles for enabling/disabling."
msgstr ""
"Los puntos de conexión de ValueSet y de reglas de negocio deben poder "
"habilitarse o deshabilitarse mediante la configuración de perfiles."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L350
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:350
msgid ""
"The WHO Global Digital Health Certification Network Secretariat is "
"responsible to manage the onboarding application of eligible Trust Network "
"Participants to connect as a trusted party to the trust network."
msgstr ""
"La Secretaría de la Red Mundial de Certificación Digital de Salud de la OMS "
"se encarga de gestionar las solicitudes de integración de los Participantes "
"en la red de confianza que reúnan los requisitos para conectarse como parte "
"de confianza a la red de confianza."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L155
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:155
msgid ""
"Therefore all raw keys must be converted to an x509 certificate wrapper to "
"be a DSC on the gateway, which must be signed by a properly onboarded SCA. "
"Verification of a COVID-19 certificate is not affected by this process, as "
"long as the correct KID is applied during the upload (and in the "
"certificate)."
msgstr ""
"Por consiguiente, todas las claves sin procesar deben convertirse en un "
"envoltorio de certificado x509 para constituir un DSC en la puerta de "
"enlace, que debe estar firmado por una SCA debidamente integrada. Este "
"proceso no afecta a la verificación de un certificado de COVID-19, siempre "
"que se aplique el KID correcto durante la carga (y en el certificado)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L17
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:17
msgid ""
"This architectural specification provides the means to establish a federated"
" trust network for use with health records like WHO Digital Documentation of"
" COVID-19 Certificates (DDCC) technical specifications and implementation "
"guidance documents. This is based on the assumption that Trust Network "
"Participant may establish their own independent national trust networks, "
"participate in a regional trust network, or wish to participate in a global "
"federated trust network. Furthermore, Trust Network Participant may wish for"
" these trust networks to be interoperable for domestic and cross-"
"jurisdictional use cases. While specific governance and policy "
"considerations required in the establishment of such interoperable trust "
"networks is out of scope of this document, the intent is that the technical "
"design within this document would support intra-jursidictional and cross-"
"jurisdictional policies of Trust Network Participant."
msgstr ""
"La presente especificación de arquitectura proporciona los medios para "
"establecer una red de confianza federada que pueda utilizarse con registros "
"de salud, como los documentos de especificaciones técnicas y orientaciones "
"de implementación de la documentación digital de certificados de COVID-19 "
"(DDCC) de la OMS. Se parte del supuesto de que los Participantes en la red "
"de confianza pueden establecer sus propias redes de confianza nacionales "
"independientes, participar en una red de confianza regional o desear "
"participar en una red de confianza federada mundial. Además, los "
"Participantes en la red de confianza pueden desear que estas redes de "
"confianza sean interoperables para casos de uso nacionales y entre "
"jurisdicciones. Si bien las consideraciones específicas de gobernanza y de "
"política que requiere el establecimiento de tales redes de confianza "
"interoperables quedan fuera del alcance del presente documento, se pretende "
"que el diseño técnico que en él se presenta apoye las políticas "
"intrajurisdiccionales y transjurisdiccionales de los Participantes en la red"
" de confianza."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L332
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:332
msgid "This section describes these changes."
msgstr "En esta sección se describen dichos cambios."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L288
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L304
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:288
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:304
msgid "Thumbprint"
msgstr "Huella digital"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L214
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:214
msgid "TimeStamp"
msgstr "TimeStamp"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L92
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:92
msgid ""
"TNG provides a way to share public keys that are used to sign digital COVID "
"certificates as well as provide lists of revoked public key certificates."
msgstr ""
"La TNG ofrece un medio para compartir las claves públicas utilizadas para "
"firmar certificados COVID digitales, así como para proporcionar listas de "
"certificados de clave pública revocados."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L82
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:82
msgid ""
"TNG provides an interoperable means for exchanging key metadata in support "
"of digital COVID-19 certificates using the HL7 FHIR standards. This "
"includes, in particular:"
msgstr ""
"La TNG ofrece un medio interoperable para intercambiar metadatos clave en "
"apoyo de los certificados de COVID-19 digitales utilizando las normas HL7 "
"FHIR. Ello incluye, en particular:"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L95
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:95
msgid ""
"TNG provides the functionality to store secure and trustful resources (i.e. "
"FHIR value sets or Business Rule) which ensures that all attendees in the "
"system have precise knowledge about important sources. These references can "
"be stored in the form of URLs."
msgstr ""
"La TNG ofrece la funcionalidad de almacenar recursos seguros y fiables (por "
"ejemplo, conjuntos de valores FHIR o reglas de negocio), lo que garantiza "
"que todos los participantes en el sistema tengan un conocimiento preciso de "
"las fuentes importantes. Estas referencias pueden almacenarse en forma de "
"URL."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L89
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:89
msgid ""
"To abstract these requirements, the Trust Network Gateway will introduce a "
"new functionality called “Trusted References”, which allows the gateway to "
"share any kind of service endpoint without sharing the content itself. For "
"backwards compatibility, the functionalities of the DCC Business Rules and "
"Value Sets remain in the architecture, but can be configured to be disabled "
"using profiles. The explicit endpoints for business rules and value sets "
"will be replaced by the trusted references, as the wide variance of medical "
"content should be left to FHIR server implementations instead of the "
"implementation of each service in the gateway itself."
msgstr ""
"Para abstraer estos requisitos, la puerta de enlace a la red de confianza "
"introducirá una nueva funcionalidad denominada «referencias de confianza», "
"que permite a la puerta de enlace compartir cualquier tipo de punto de "
"conexión de servicio sin compartir el contenido en sí. A efectos de "
"compatibilidad con versiones anteriores, las funcionalidades de reglas de "
"negocio y conjuntos de valores del DCC se mantienen en la arquitectura, pero"
" pueden deshabilitarse mediante perfiles. Los puntos de conexión explícitos "
"para reglas de negocio y conjuntos de valores se sustituirán por las "
"referencias de confianza, ya que la gran variabilidad del contenido médico "
"debería dejarse en manos de las implementaciones de servidores FHIR, en "
"lugar de implementar cada servicio en la propia puerta de enlace."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L71
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:71
msgid ""
"To establish the trust between attendees, a trust mediator can be generated "
"which relies on the trustlist of the gateway. The mediator can then use this"
" information to decide whether the trust relationship should be established "
"or not. For instance, the interceptor can check if a signature of a JWT was "
"created by the public key of a certificate which was signed by an onboarded "
"SCA. When the SCA is onboarded and trusted, it proves that the signature was"
" made by someone which has the trust of this SCA. The trust for this "
"attendee is then also given."
msgstr ""
"Para establecer la confianza entre participantes, puede crearse un mediador "
"de confianza que se base en la lista de confianza de la puerta de enlace. A "
"continuación, el mediador puede utilizar esta información para decidir si "
"debería establecerse o no la relación de confianza. Por ejemplo, el "
"interceptor puede comprobar si la firma de un JWT se creó con la clave "
"pública de un certificado firmado por una SCA integrada. Si la SCA está "
"integrada y es de confianza, ello demuestra que la firma fue realizada por "
"alguien que cuenta con la confianza de dicha SCA. En ese caso, también se "
"otorga la confianza a ese participante."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L246
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:246
msgid ""
"To federate multiple gateway data, a download process is introduced which "
"should ensure that only trusted data is downloaded to a local gateway. "
"Trusted data means in this context, that the operator of a local gateway has"
" the total control which federated data is accepted and which not. To "
"achieve this target, the local gateway operator must explicitly onboard any "
"remote federators plus the trust anchors of the data which can be accepted. "
"This is necessary because each remote federator may deliver the data of "
"multiple other gateways (which are trusted by the origin gateway operator), "
"but this means not necessarily that this data is trusted automatically by "
"the local gateway operator as well (implicit trust relations must be "
"avoided). Therefore, during the download process, a check should be run "
"which skips all data that is not explicitly trusted by the local operator. "
"This can be reached over the whitelisting of multiple trust anchors and the "
"cross check over the TNPUP certificates. If the trust chain is established "
"in this way, each content can be downloaded, verified and pushed to the "
"store. The entire download process itself follows a delta download "
"mechanism, which downloads daily the entire content, and within the day just"
" the deltas. This means for the trust network, that a certificate “bubbles” "
"from the origin gateway step by step to all other gateways. Through this "
"behavior, it must be considered that around one day between creating a key "
"pair, and issuing the first certificates with it is considered."
msgstr ""
"Para federar los datos de varias puertas de enlace, se introduce un proceso "
"de descarga que debería garantizar que solo se descarguen datos de confianza"
" en una puerta de enlace local. En este contexto, por datos de confianza se "
"entiende que el operador de una puerta de enlace local tiene pleno control "
"sobre qué datos federados se aceptan y cuáles no. Para lograr este objetivo,"
" el operador de la puerta de enlace local debe integrar explícitamente "
"cualquier federador remoto, además de las anclas de confianza de los datos "
"que puedan aceptarse. Ello es necesario porque cada federador remoto puede "
"entregar los datos de muchas otras puertas de enlace (en las que confía el "
"operador de la puerta de enlace de origen), lo que no significa "
"necesariamente que el operador de la puerta de enlace local confíe también "
"automáticamente en esos datos (deben evitarse las relaciones de confianza "
"implícitas). Por consiguiente, durante el proceso de descarga debería "
"realizarse una comprobación que omita todos los datos en los que el operador"
" local no confíe explícitamente. Ello puede lograrse mediante la inclusión "
"en listas blancas de varias anclas de confianza y la verificación cruzada a "
"través de los certificados TNPUP. Si la cadena de confianza se establece de "
"este modo, cada contenido puede descargarse, verificarse e introducirse en "
"el almacén. El proceso de descarga en su conjunto sigue un mecanismo de "
"descarga diferencial, que descarga diariamente todo el contenido y, a lo "
"largo del día, solo las diferencias. Para la red de confianza, esto "
"significa que un certificado se propaga paso a paso desde la puerta de "
"enlace de origen a todas las demás puertas de enlace. Debido a este "
"comportamiento, debe tenerse en cuenta que transcurre aproximadamente un día"
" entre la creación de un par de claves y la expedición de los primeros "
"certificados con él."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L265
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:265
msgid ""
"To monitor the status of the Gateway, a health check is introduced. The new "
"route returns 200 if the gateway is up and running. When the gateway is in "
"maintenance, the routes must return 204. All other return codes indicate an "
"error."
msgstr ""
"Para supervisar el estado de la puerta de enlace, se introduce una "
"comprobación del estado. La nueva ruta devuelve 200 si la puerta de enlace "
"está activa y en funcionamiento. Cuando la puerta de enlace está en "
"mantenimiento, las rutas deben devolver 204. Todos los demás códigos de "
"retorno indican un error."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L101
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:101
msgid ""
"To realize the architectural vision, the existing DCC Gateway will be "
"enhanced by a microservice which implements the TNG Federator component. "
"This federator component is deployed next to the gateway and it handles the "
"communication with other federators. Each federator is able to download the "
"data of other components. Uploading the data to other federators is not "
"foreseen (each gateway downloads over a federator). The trusted consumers "
"can decide to use the federation information and must explicitly activate "
"this feature. To summarize, the federator acts as a gateway "
"connector/synchronizer and as an interface provider for accessing the "
"federated data."
msgstr ""
"Para hacer realidad la visión de la arquitectura, la puerta de enlace del "
"DCC existente se ampliará con un microservicio que implementa el componente "
"federador de la TNG. Este componente federador se despliega junto a la "
"puerta de enlace y gestiona la comunicación con otros federadores. Cada "
"federador puede descargar los datos de otros componentes. No está prevista "
"la carga de datos en otros federadores (cada puerta de enlace descarga a "
"través de un federador). Los consumidores de confianza pueden decidir "
"utilizar la información de federación y deben activar explícitamente esta "
"funcionalidad. En resumen, el federador actúa como conector/sincronizador de"
" puertas de enlace y como proveedor de interfaz para acceder a los datos "
"federados."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L142
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:142
msgid ""
"To realize the architecture vision, the gateway trust model will be enhanced"
" so that the federator can support multiple trust anchors. For this purpose,"
" the TNG Federator will be onboarded in the source gateway with an TNPTLS "
"and TNPUP certificate to access the gateway content. In the destination "
"gateway, the trust anchor of the source gateway is configured (and signed by"
" the operator) to accept the source content as valid. If the verification is"
" successful, the content will be added as a subset to the existing gateway "
"content. The connected national backends can then download all information "
"by activating the federation option, to get the content from both gateways. "
"The trust chain can be verified about the trust anchor of the connected "
"gateway and the trust list of onboarded trust anchors."
msgstr ""
"Para hacer realidad la visión de la arquitectura, el modelo de confianza de "
"la puerta de enlace se ampliará de modo que el federador pueda admitir "
"varias anclas de confianza. Con este fin, el federador de la TNG se "
"integrará en la puerta de enlace de origen con un certificado TNPTLS y un "
"certificado TNPUP para acceder al contenido de la puerta de enlace. En la "
"puerta de enlace de destino, se configura el ancla de confianza de la puerta"
" de enlace de origen (firmada por el operador) para aceptar como válido el "
"contenido de origen. Si la verificación tiene éxito, el contenido se añadirá"
" como subconjunto al contenido existente de la puerta de enlace. A "
"continuación, los sistemas de back-end nacionales conectados pueden "
"descargar toda la información activando la opción de federación, para "
"obtener el contenido de ambas puertas de enlace. La cadena de confianza "
"puede verificarse mediante el ancla de confianza de la puerta de enlace "
"conectada y la lista de confianza de las anclas de confianza integradas."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L128
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:128
msgid ""
"To sign digital COVID-19 certificates, a Document Signer Certificate (“DSC”)"
" is created by an issuing authority. Each authority distributes their DSCs "
"to verifiers, so that DSC can be used to prove the validity of an issued "
"certificate. To establish a trust chain between used DSCs and the "
"distributors of the national trust lists, each of the DSC is signed by a "
"root authority (“SCA”) to verify the authenticity of the DSC itself. For "
"security reasons, the SCA is declared as air gapped, and the public part is "
"later on-boarded into the gateway. During the onboarding, the SCA is signed "
"by the operator of the gateway to give the trust in the initial check. After"
" onboarding, each incoming DSC can be checked against the trusted SCA. The "
"operator signature (signed by DCCGTA) establishes the trust with different "
"certificates such as the uploader certificate and the TLS authentication "
"certificate as defined by the certificate governance."
msgstr ""
"Para firmar certificados de COVID-19 digitales, una autoridad emisora crea "
"un certificado de firmante de documentos («DSC»). Cada autoridad distribuye "
"sus DSC a los verificadores, de modo que el DSC pueda utilizarse para "
"demostrar la validez de un certificado expedido. Para establecer una cadena "
"de confianza entre los DSC utilizados y los distribuidores de las listas de "
"confianza nacionales, cada DSC es firmado por una autoridad raíz («SCA») a "
"fin de verificar la autenticidad del propio DSC. Por motivos de seguridad, "
"la SCA se declara aislada de la red (air gapped), y su parte pública se "
"integra posteriormente en la puerta de enlace. Durante la integración, la "
"SCA es firmada por el operador de la puerta de enlace para otorgar la "
"confianza en la comprobación inicial. Tras la integración, cada DSC entrante"
" puede comprobarse con respecto a la SCA de confianza. La firma del operador"
" (firmada por DCCGTA) establece la confianza con distintos certificados, "
"como el certificado de carga y el certificado de autenticación TLS, según lo"
" definido en la gobernanza de certificados."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L262
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:262
msgid ""
"To support additional use cases, the gateway will be modified with endpoints"
" which allows it to upload certificates signed by the SCA of a Trust Network"
" Partcipant. The upload endpoint works similar to the signer information "
"upload endpoint with the difference that the upload contains more additional"
" information about the certificate. The concrete template for this "
"additional information must be defined by a schema. The certificate upload "
"must support the choice of a kid, because other standards define static kids"
" or choose it in other ways than the DCC. If no kid is provided, the DCC "
"standard calculation of the first 8 bytes of the SHA256 hash is applied."
msgstr ""
"Para dar soporte a casos de uso adicionales, la puerta de enlace se "
"modificará con puntos de conexión que permitan cargar certificados firmados "
"por la SCA de un Participante en la red de confianza. El punto de conexión "
"de carga funciona de manera similar al punto de conexión de carga de "
"información de firmantes, con la diferencia de que la carga contiene más "
"información adicional sobre el certificado. La plantilla concreta para esta "
"información adicional debe definirse mediante un esquema. La carga de "
"certificados debe permitir elegir un kid, ya que otras normas definen kid "
"estáticos o los eligen de formas distintas a las del DCC. Si no se "
"proporciona ningún kid, se aplica el cálculo estándar del DCC de los "
"primeros 8 bytes del hash SHA256."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L133
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:133
msgid ""
"To support multiple content in the gateway in the same security level, the "
"trust model introduces CMS as a generic container for security relevant "
"items. The CMS format allows it to standardize signing and encryption "
"regardless of the content, for single or multiple recipients."
msgstr ""
"Para admitir distintos contenidos en la puerta de enlace con el mismo nivel "
"de seguridad, el modelo de confianza introduce CMS como contenedor genérico "
"para los elementos relevantes para la seguridad. El formato CMS permite "
"normalizar la firma y el cifrado con independencia del contenido, para uno o"
" varios destinatarios."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L336
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:336
msgid ""
"To support the DID document feature according to the trust specification, "
"the gateway will be enhanced by a DID document generator and the capability "
"to sign these DID documents. This contains a way to generate signing keys "
"over a vault and register the public key of the signature over a "
"decentralized key registry."
msgstr ""
"Para dar soporte a la funcionalidad de documentos DID conforme a la "
"especificación de confianza, la puerta de enlace se ampliará con un "
"generador de documentos DID y la capacidad de firmar dichos documentos DID. "
"Ello incluye un medio para generar claves de firma a través de un almacén "
"seguro (vault) y registrar la clave pública de la firma en un registro "
"descentralizado de claves."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md#L220
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/trust_network_gateway_architecture.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_network_gateway_architecture.md:220
msgid ""
"To use the federated data, the gateway will be enhanced by federation "
"endpoints which are modified variants of the common GET routes. By using "
"this new endpoints, the common content is modified returned:"
msgstr ""
"Para utilizar los datos federados, la puerta de enlace se ampliará con "
"puntos de conexión de federación, que son variantes modificadas de las rutas"
" GET comunes. Al utilizar estos nuevos puntos de conexión, el contenido "
"común se devuelve modificado:"

